# Weaver — environment. Copy to .env and fill in.
#
# You do not need this file to start. With nothing configured, Weaver picks a
# free, keyless endpoint (Pollinations). If a key below is already in your
# environment, Weaver finds it and uses that provider instead — that is how it
# "just works" on a machine that has any of these set.
#
#   weaver providers     every endpoint, and which keys are present
#   weaver setup         pick one and paste a key
#   weaver models        what the active provider actually offers
#
# Everything in this file is optional.

# Force a provider instead of auto-detecting.
# One of: pollinations | groq | gemini | openrouter | ollama | openai | together | mock
# WEAVER_PROVIDER=groq

# Model id. Leave unset for the provider's default. List them with `weaver models`.
# WEAVER_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-120b

# API keys. Only the one for the provider you actually use is needed, and the
# keyless ones (pollinations, ollama) plus mock need none at all.
GROQ_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# TOGETHER_API_KEY=

# A key that works for whatever provider is selected.
# WEAVER_API_KEY=

# Point at any OpenAI-compatible endpoint (overrides the provider preset).
# WEAVER_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# Where the agent is allowed to work. Defaults to the current directory.
# WEAVER_WORKSPACE=.

# Where Weaver keeps sessions and config.json. Defaults to ~/.weaver
# WEAVER_HOME=./.weaver

# Permission gate: auto (ask before writes/shell) | full (never ask) | readonly (never write)
# WEAVER_PERMISSION=auto

# Canary sign-off: auto (run after changes) | off
# WEAVER_CANARY=auto

# Cap on model calls per turn. Defaults to 24.
# WEAVER_MAX_STEPS=24

# Point the sign-off at a different engine, or a different CLI on PATH.
# WEAVER_CANARY_ENGINE=../zabibu-canary/packages/engine/src/index.ts
# WEAVER_CANARY_CLI=zabibucanary
